One harsh season, a repaired caravan halted at the edge of town, its master worn by scarcity and pride. He offered coin for any shortcut to fortune, threatening to sell the caravan’s last memory to survive. Elin listened to the desert wind and chose a different gift: she shared her map and offered to guide the caravan, not to the nearest gold but to the wellsprings hidden beneath the town’s oldest stones.

